# Desktop build of the wgrender simple example.
#
# Run `./build.py desktop`: it builds wgrender's desktop library, then writes
# build/<os>/<variant>/build.hxml (build/linux/release/, ...): this file, where wgrender
# is on this machine and how to link it, and the target, --cpp build/<os>/<variant>/cpp.
# Once that has run, `haxe build/linux/release/build.hxml` works on its own; it just
# won't rebuild wgrender.

-cp src
-lib wgrender-hx
--main Simple
# hxcpp names the binary after this (default: the main class).
-D HAXE_OUTPUT_FILE=simple
# 64-bit on every OS: hxcpp builds 32-bit on Windows unless told otherwise
-D HXCPP_M64

-dce full
-D analyzer-optimize
